            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR corrects many JS code problems that are code style guide violations.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Note that many of these are to add assignments to variables that are used. I know the examples explicitly say they are incomplete, but making them just a little bit more self-contained is certainly useful, especially if it's not immediately apparent how you can initialize them.</p>",
