        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22709264?u=a10979e7969de88f4862300d32505942cd748097&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h2 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h2>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Remove the duplicated <code class=\"notranslate\">property</code> in the Grid auto-placement guide.</li>\n<li>No technical or behavioral changes.</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45855",
            "title": "docs(css): remove duplicate \"property\" in grid auto-placement guide",
            "date_modified": "2026-09-26T10:43:16.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-09-26T10:41:40.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Rawal27",
                "url": "https://github.com/Rawal27"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/236759479?u=6a2b51441b1015f9a4beae865bfcb3f1a2ea9899&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The Values section listed the one-, two- and three-value combinations of <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;number&gt;</code> and explained <code class=\"notranslate\">auto</code> in a paragraph below them. This lists <code class=\"notranslate\">auto</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;integer&gt;</code> as the two entries, with the position rules (and what an omitted second or third value becomes) under <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;integer&gt;</code>, as suggested in the review of <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4992022479\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44937\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/44937/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44937\">#44937</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It also changes <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;number&gt;</code> to <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;integer&gt;</code>: the spec grammar is <code class=\"notranslate\">[ auto | &lt;integer [0,∞]&gt; ]{1,3}</code>, and non-integers are rejected.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">auto</code> was the only value not in the definition list, and <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;number&gt;</code> suggested that values like <code class=\"notranslate\">1.5</code> are allowed.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Spec: <a href=\"https://drafts.csswg.org/css-text-4/#propdef-hyphenate-limit-chars\" rel=\"nofollow\">CSS Text 4, <code class=\"notranslate\">hyphenate-limit-chars</code></a> (\"If the third value is missing, it is the same as the second. If the second value is missing, then it is auto.\")</li>\n<li>WPT <a href=\"https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/css/css-text/parsing/hyphenate-limit-chars-invalid.html\"><code class=\"notranslate\">hyphenate-limit-chars-invalid.html</code></a> treats <code class=\"notranslate\">1.2</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">1 1.2</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">1 2 1.2</code> as invalid.</li>\n<li>Checked in headless Edge 153 with <code class=\"notranslate\">CSS.supports(\"hyphenate-limit-chars\", …)</code>: <code class=\"notranslate\">10</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">10 4</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">10 4 4</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">auto 3</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">10 auto 4</code> are true; <code class=\"notranslate\">1.2</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">10.0</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">10 4.5</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">10 4 4.5</code> are false.</li>\n<li>markdownlint-cli2, prettier and cspell pass on the file.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #45071.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5112357853\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45071\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45071/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45071\">#45071</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45854",
            "title": "hyphenate-limit-chars: list auto and <integer> as separate values",
            "date_modified": "2026-09-26T09:27:00.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-09-26T09:24:43.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "RizgarOzan",
                "url": "https://github.com/RizgarOzan"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Turns out that there's simply no way to tell if a PWA is running as an installed app.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #34928.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2419254063\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/34928\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/34928/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/34928\">#34928</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45852",
            "title": "Remove guidance to use display-mode to infer PWA installation status",
            "date_modified": "2026-09-25T21:58:24.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-09-25T21:56:50.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Josh-Cena",
                "url": "https://github.com/Josh-Cena"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96150?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I've added a one-line note that, on Windows, <code class=\"notranslate\">font-family: cursive</code> means Comic Sans MS.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It's an unfortunate quirk of the web that Chrome, Edge, Firefox, and Opera all render <code class=\"notranslate\">font-family: cursive</code> using Comic Sans MS on Windows.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">MDN indicates that <code class=\"notranslate\">cursive</code> implies that the glyphs would be at least partially connected by joining strokes, but Comic Sans MS doesn't connect any of its glyphs. IMO, Comic Sans MS is not \"cursive,\" at all.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I was caught very much by surprise when I used <code class=\"notranslate\">font-family: cursive</code> and tested on iOS, Android, and macOS, and got Apple Chancery on iOS/macOS and Dancing Script on Android, but got Comic Sans MS on all browsers on Windows. (Comic Sans MS has a casual, comedic vibe. It was very much <em>not</em> what I was going for when I selected <code class=\"notranslate\">font-family: cursive</code>.)</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If a note like this had appeared on MDN, it would have saved me some embarrassment.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45851",
            "title": "Document that `font-family: cursive` is Comic Sans MS on Windows",
            "date_modified": "2026-09-25T21:41:50.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-09-25T21:28:28.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "dfabulich",
                "url": "https://github.com/dfabulich"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69888?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">The <code class=\"notranslate\">@supports</code> was missing from the first example.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45849",
            "title": "Add @supports to column-height property",
            "date_modified": "2026-09-25T13:48:48.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-09-25T13:07:34.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "estelle",
                "url": "https://github.com/estelle"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/143684587?u=5439f94a2cf31212e19f179d4defd1344c321579&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds a \"Channel values outside the output range\" subsection to the \"Using relative colors\" guide, with a worked <code class=\"notranslate\">display-p3</code> example showing that channel values beyond the output function's range are used as they are, not clamped or gamut-mapped.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The guide explains that channel values resolve to <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;number&gt;</code> values, but not what happens when the origin color lies outside the output function's gamut. Readers who compute <code class=\"notranslate\">rgb()</code> relative colors from wide-gamut origins see values above <code class=\"notranslate\">255</code>, and a <code class=\"notranslate\">color(srgb ...)</code> serialization, with nothing on the page explaining either.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The example is the one <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/romainmenke/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/romainmenke\">@romainmenke</a> suggested in the issue, kept inside the display-p3 gamut as recommended there. Values checked in Chromium 151:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">rgb(from color(display-p3 1 0.5 0.5) r g b)</code> computes to <code class=\"notranslate\">color(srgb 1.07398 0.462581 0.483011)</code>, so <code class=\"notranslate\">r</code> is about <code class=\"notranslate\">273.86</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">rgb(from color(display-p3 1 0.5 0.5) calc(r - 1) g b)</code> computes to <code class=\"notranslate\">color(srgb 1.07006 0.462581 0.483011)</code></li>\n<li>the absolute <code class=\"notranslate\">rgb(272.86 117.96 123.17)</code> computes to <code class=\"notranslate\">rgb(255, 118, 123)<span class=\"ml-1 d-inline-block border circle color-border-subtle\" style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 118, 123); height: 8px; width: 8px;\"></span></code>, clamped</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Spec: <a href=\"https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color-5/#relative-colors\" rel=\"nofollow\">CSS Color 5, relative color syntax</a>.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #32704.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2189521620\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/32704\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/32704/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/32704\">#32704</a><br>\nRelates to <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2107524745\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/32004\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/32004/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/32004\">#32004</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45847",
            "title": "CSS relative colors: explain channel values outside the output range",
            "date_modified": "2026-09-25T12:12:23.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-09-25T12:11:56.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hipuku",
                "url": "https://github.com/hipuku"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5276969?u=8cddfa087ad4d174b236980e19ecf5254320f529&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Changes for WebDriver conformance for the Firefox 157 release are based on the <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/buglist.cgi?o2=notequals&amp;v4=%5Bwebdriver%3Arelnote%5D&amp;resolution=FIXED&amp;v1=fixed&amp;f2=cf_status_firefox156&amp;product=Remote%20Protocol&amp;v3=%5Bwptsync%20downstream%5D&amp;f4=status_whiteboard&amp;list_id=18128491&amp;query_format=advanced&amp;o1=equals&amp;o3=notsubstring&amp;component=Agent&amp;component=Marionette&amp;component=WebDriver%20BiDi&amp;columnlist=component%2Cresolution%2Cassigned_to%2Cshort_desc%2Cbug_type%2Cstatus_whiteboard&amp;f1=cf_status_firefox157&amp;o4=substring&amp;v2=fixed&amp;f3=status_whiteboard\" rel=\"nofollow\">release-worthy bugs in this list</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45845",
